records.problem:
In the sequence $\{a_n\}$, $a_1=4$, $na_{n+1}-(n+1)a_n=2n^2+2n$.
(Ⅰ) Prove that the sequence $\left\{ \frac{a_n}{n} \right\}$ is an arithmetic sequence;
(Ⅱ) Find the sum of the first $n$ terms, $S_n$, of the sequence $\left\{ \frac{1}{a_n} \right\}$.
